Falsifies `non_volatile_memory_express::verification::capabilities_decode_is_total_and_reads_the_specified_bits`.

The defect: `Capabilities::doorbell_stride` masks five bits instead of the register's four, so bit 36 of
the register (a reserved bit) leaks into the stride and the stride can reach 31. `doorbell` masks it
back to four bits, so the damage would be a quietly wrong offset rather than a panic.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(capabilities.doorbell_stride() <= 15)`.

diff --git a/src/capabilities.rs b/src/capabilities.rs
index 30ddda8..aac3b73 100644
--- a/src/capabilities.rs
+++ b/src/capabilities.rs
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ impl Capabilities {
     /// Doorbell Stride: doorbell N is at `0x1000 + N * (4 << DSTRD)` (a 4-bit field, so the shift
     /// is at most 19 and the multiply cannot overflow a u64 for any real doorbell index).
     pub fn doorbell_stride(self) -> u32 {
-        (self.0 >> 32) as u32 & 0xf
+        (self.0 >> 32) as u32 & 0x1f
     }
     /// Timeout for the ready bit to follow the enable bit, in units of 500 milliseconds.
     #[doc(alias = "CAP.TO")]
